Our progress -

We created a CardsPanel class using Java Swing to display the cards known to the player. The panel is divided into 
three categories: People, Rooms, and Weapons. Each category has separate sections for cards in the player's hand 
and cards they have seen. We used GridLayout and BoxLayout to organize the different sections and added titled 
borders to make the panel easier to read. We also implemented a method to update the displayed cards and show 
"None" when no cards are available. We included a main method to test the panel independently in a JFrame.
The panel currently displays correctly using placeholder information, but we still need to connect it to the 
player's actual hand and seen cards. Our next step is to integrate it into the Minecraft-themed Clue game alongside 
the game control panel.
